  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Ken. I've verified your identity as an authorized user on Mei's account, and I found order 8901 from Kaze Sushi. The salmon roll ($9.50) was delivered on tonight's order, and I can see it was reported within the required window.\n\nI'm not able to send that refund to the Visa card, though. As an authorized user, any compensation for this order has to go to the account as store credit. Here's what I can offer:\n\n- **Account credit of $11.40** for the salmon roll (the $9.50 item price plus 20%), usable on future Forkful orders.\n\nWould you like me to add the $11.40 credit to Mei's account? Please confirm and I'll process it."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Wait, why can't it go back to the card? I'd rather have it on the card than as credit."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I understand you'd rather have the money back on your card. The policy is specific here: when an authorized user like you reports a problem, any compensation has to be account credit, not a refund to the card. Only the account holder can have refunds sent to the original payment method, and that's a limit I can't override.\n\nYour options are:\n\n- **Account credit of $11.40** on Mei's account, which is the item price plus 20%. It's usable on any future Forkful order.\n- **Ask Mei to contact us herself.** As the account holder, she can request a refund to the card. I can verify her separately if she reaches out.\n\nWould you like me to add the $11.40 credit, or would you prefer to have Mei contact us about the card refund?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, I'll take the credit then. Go ahead and add the $11.40 to Mei's account. Thanks for sorting it out."
  },
